            <ArticleTitle>Imaging manifestations of Behcet's disease: Key considerations and major features.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>214-225</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0720-048X(17)30502-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ejrad.2017.11.012</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Behcet's disease is an autoimmune disease most commonly seen in the Middle East. Although primarily known with painful oral and genital ulcers, it can lead to vasculitis. Therefore, several associated complications such as thrombotic syndromes, aneurysmal arterial disease may arise. In many cases, it might be difficult to make the diagnosis purely based on clinical grounds; however, imaging plays an important role for both diagnosis and assessment of the disease's complications. We provide a comprehensive review of the most notable imaging findings of Behcet's disease.</AbstractText>
